# Versioning & Changelog

Follow [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/) and [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/).

## Version format

- Pre-1.0: `0.MINOR.PATCH` — breaking changes may bump MINOR until 1.0.0
- From 1.0: MAJOR for breaking, MINOR for features, PATCH for fixes

## When to update

On every user-visible or architecturally meaningful change:

1. Add entries under `## [Unreleased]` in `CHANGELOG.md`
2. Bump version in `package.json` only when cutting a release (not every commit)

## Changelog entries

- Sections: `Added`, `Changed`, `Fixed`, `Removed`, `Deprecated`, `Security`
- Write for users/learners and contributors — what changed and why it matters
- One bullet per logical change; link issues/PRs when available
- Omit empty sections in releases

## Release workflow

When the user asks to release or tag a version:

1. Move `[Unreleased]` items to `## [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD`
2. Add fresh empty `## [Unreleased]` at top
3. Set `package.json` `"version"` to `X.Y.Z`
4. Commit: `release: vX.Y.Z`

## Do not

- Skip changelog updates for features, fixes, or breaking changes
- Use vague entries ("misc updates", "WIP")
- Let `package.json` version drift from the latest CHANGELOG release
